	(text_box "TPS2116 Power Multiplexer\nAllows for automatic selection between two 5V sources to power the MIDI keyboard (VBUS_KBD).\n\nVIN1 (VBUS_IN) is given priority. When USB is plugged in, the keyboard is powered directly from the USB 5V rail, preserving battery life and allowing for the battery to charge.\n\nWhen USB is disconnected, the IC automatically switches to VIN2 (BOOST_5V) which is generated by the MT3608 boost converter from the LiPo battery.\n\nThe PR1 resistor divider (R13=100kΩ, R14=27kΩ) sets the switchover threshold at ~4.7V on VIN1. When VBUS_IN drops below this threshold the IC switches to battery power within microseconds with no interruption to the keyboard.\n\nThe ST pin outputs the current active source and is routed to ESP32 IO38 so firmware can detect whether the device is USB or battery powered."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
